# Swift package build artifacts (regenerated by swift/build-xcframework.sh).
#
# SWIFT-2 (issue #110): these rules live on `main` even though `swift/` does
# not, and that is deliberate — landing them AHEAD of the binding is the whole
# point. The Swift/UniFFI binding is still on the unmerged `design/swift-binding`
# branch, which carries these same rules; on `main` they had no effect, so a
# working tree that had ever built the binding showed a bare `?? swift/` of
# ~974 MB — `.build/`, `.xcbuild/`, and a `Chisel.xcframework/` holding three
# prebuilt static archives — with nothing ignoring any of it. One `git add -A`
# commits the lot into history, which is not recoverable without a rewrite.
# Ignoring them here means that stops being possible the moment the binding
# arrives, rather than one merge later.
swift/Chisel.xcframework/
swift/.build/
swift/.xcbuild/
swift/*.o
swift/*.d
swift/*.swiftdeps
swift/*.swiftdeps~
